<title>JAPAN: Japan economy growing gradually, more solid -- MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan economy growing gradually, more solid -- MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's economy is gradually growing and increasing in solidness, Minister of Finance Hiroshi Mitsuzuka told a news conference on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>&quot;The economy is finally on a gradual growth track and becoming more solid,&quot; Mitsuzuka said.</p>
<p>Asked about talks on an insurance dispute with the United States due to resume on Thursday, the minister said the two sides were still unable to agree on basic issues.</p>
<p>&quot;The (U.S.-Japan) ministerial meeting on December 14 will be the final one; we basically have to decide by this deadline,&quot; Mitsuzuka said, referring to talks scheduled between himself and acting U.S. Trade Representative Charlene Barshefsky.  </p>
<p>The two countries have been at odds over deregulation of Japan's domestic insurance market.</p>
